  "published": "2026-08-21T15:01:43.833Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.0\nBREAKING: maxBodyDuration is now a required constructor parameter on every coordinator\n  (EphemeralWorkCoordinator, EphemeralKeyedWorkCoordinator, EphemeralResultCoordinator,\n  PriorityWorkCoordinator/PriorityKeyedWorkCoordinator). A body whose Task never resolves\n  previously held its concurrency slot forever, silently -- confirmed as the cause of a real\n  ~20-hour production wedge. No default is provided on purpose; see BREAKING_CHANGES_3.0.md\n  for migration guidance, including a positional-argument hazard worth reading first.\nNEW: BodyDurationGuard bounds body execution via Task.WaitAsync against an injectable\n  TimeProvider. Trips loudly: signal \"coordinator.body.timeout\", typed\n  BodyDurationExceededException, freed concurrency slot.\nFIXED: Polly PackageReference removed from Mostlylucid.Notify (licensing; was unused).\n\nv2.0.0\nBREAKING: SignalRaised event removed - use Subscribe() instead\nBREAKING: .NET 6.0/7.0 removed - minimum is .NET 8.0\n\nNEW: Detection Ledger System for evidence accumulation\n- DetectionLedger aggregates detector contributions with sigmoid function\n- DetectionContribution with factory methods (Bot, Human, VerifiedBot, etc.)\n- CategoryScore breakdown for explainability\n- IEntityLedger generic interface for any entity type\n- LedgerSignal with salience and provenance metadata\n\nNEW: Lock-free Signal Subscription\n- sink.Subscribe(handler) returns IDisposable\n- Pattern-based forwarding: errorSink.SubscribeToPattern(mainSink, \"error.*\")\n\nNEW: WindowSizeAtom for dynamic capacity management via signals\nSECURITY: Patched System.Text.Json and Npgsql vulnerabilities\nPERF: Bounded cleanup iteration prevents degradation under load",
